  "transformations": [
    "Principal native API made internal; common Encoder/Decoder is the public surface.",
    "In-house MIT identifiers normalised to Apache-2.0 under the recorded owner decision.",
    "Accelerate imports and CoreGraphics comparator guarded; Linux scalar primitives and ICC MD5 added.",
    "Shared lossless kernels gain row-bounded cancellation and serial operation execution.",
    "Native parser is preceded by bounded marker-envelope validation.",
    "DICOM reader/writer and optional Apple window comparator retained only in the test target for frozen container regressions; no DICOM shipping product added.",
    "Contract-layer regression assertions adapted through a test-only public async API bridge; marker-valid truncated entropy exercises post-borrow invalidation.",
    "Synthetic benchmark generators, baseline helpers and identity matrix retained in test support. Native version-shape assertion is covered by successor VERSION/CLI checks.",
    "Scalar DSP now compiles on every platform; task-local kernel dispatch selects scalar or Apple Accelerate. Byte conversion follows Accelerate nearest-even ties. Operation-owned native work remains serial to retain backend/cancellation context.",
    "DCT kernels accept borrowed source/final destination storage, with row-sized colour scratch, bounded DCT/trellis batches and throwing cancellation checks. Progressive input validation rejects unsupported topology and invalid approximation history; DC predictor arithmetic is checked.",
    "Public reduced-scale and raw greyscale Float32 output use the native DCT planes directly; full-frame workspace is admitted before preview decode. Adaptive field computations now propagate bounded cancellation and are exposed through explicit validated DCT options."
